CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ one element: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ two elements: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ empty: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [temp.variadic]/5, [dcl.fct]/8: `decltype(fat(a...))' in f's trailing
return type expands the function parameter pack, one argument per element.
instantiate_template replicated the pack parameter (a$0, a$1) and expanded
the body, but not the trailing return type (by then the declaration's
type), so for two elements decltype(f(1, 'c')) was tup<int> (bin53).
Related: a short name was taken as an empty pack whenever any bound pack
of that name was empty, also an older one of another template
(guess_function_template_args; libc++'s __bind_back,
cpp20_views_take_bind_back_forward_not_found).  g++ 13 and clang++ 18
accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
